Subject: [PATCH 11/18] fix: address code quality issues in logging module

Fix multiple code quality issues reported by static analysis:

1. Header inclusion order (G.INC.07-CPP):
   - Reorder to: libobmm_log.h, vendor_adaptor.h, libobmm.h
   - Log header first, then vendor adaptor, then main module header

2. Magic numbers (G.CNS.02-CPP):
   - Add NSEC_PER_MSEC (1000000) constant
   - Add MSEC_PER_SEC (1000) constant
   - Replace magic numbers with named constants

3. Unsafe function usage (G.FUU.21):
   - Replace strcat() with bounded snprintf()
   - Calculate remaining buffer size before appending
   - Remove unused NODE_STR_BUFFER_SIZE macro

4. Variable declaration style (G.FMT.04-CPP):
   - Split 'int fd, ret;' into separate declarations
   - One variable per line for clarity

5. Parameter formatting (G.FMT.06-CPP):
   - Fix snprintf parameter indentation to 16 spaces (standard)
   - Align multi-line function calls consistently

These changes improve code safety and maintainability without
changing functionality.
